# Plan Workflow

When the user asks to create a plan:

- Save the plan in `docs/plans/` of the repository that owns the requested work.
- If `docs/plans/` does not exist, create it in that repository.
- Name the file `YYYY_MM_DD_HH-MM_<branch-slug>_<plan-title>.plan.md`.
- Use local current time for `YYYY_MM_DD_HH-MM`.
- Build `<branch-slug>` from the current git branch by replacing `/` with `__`.
- Normalize `<plan-title>` to lowercase ASCII kebab-case.
- Include the goal, scope, files to create/modify, execution tasks, and validation steps.
- For engine work, prefer validation with `npm test` and, when relevant, `npm run build` or `npm run test:build`.
- If the user asks to execute the plan, append a final implementation/build report to the same plan file with changed files, validation evidence, and limitations.
- Do not create commits unless the user explicitly asks.
